- **Description:** A palindrome reads the same forwards and backwards.
- **C Code:**
  ```c
  #include <stdio.h>
  #include <string.h>

  int is_palindrome(const char* str) {
      int left = 0;
      int right = strlen(str) - 1;

      while (left < right) {
          if (str[left] != str[right]) {
              return 0; // Not a palindrome
          }
          left++;
          right--;
      }
      return 1; // Is a palindrome
  }

  int main() {
      const char* test1 = "madam";
      const char* test2 = "hello";

      printf("%s is %spalindrome\n", test1, is_palindrome(test1) ? "" : "not ");
      printf("%s is %spalindrome\n", test2, is_palindrome(test2) ? "" : "not ");

      return 0;
  }
  ```
- **Algorithm Steps:**
  - Initialize two pointers at the start and end of the string.
  - Compare characters moving towards the center.
  - If any pair doesn't match, return false.
  - If all pairs match, return true.

